jobs.description:
Are you looking for an active job with variety in your tasks? FedEx in Duiven is looking for logistic employees. Your job is to make sure that all packages will reach their destination in time.

Your hourly salary can be €21,22 including shift allowance.

What are you going to do?
In this dynamic role, you'll ensure the smooth running of the sorting process. Your duties include:

• Sorting and processing incoming packages;

• Efficiently loading packages onto trucks;

• Collaborating with colleagues to meet deadlines.

You'll work the following shifts:

2:30 PM – 11:00 PM

5:30 PM – 1:00 AM

11:00 PM – 7:00 AM

What do we offer?
• Gross hourly wage of €15,16, with allowances up to €21,22 per hour;

• Prospects of permanent employment with FedEx;

• 8% holiday allowance and 25 vacation days;

• Travel allowance of €0,25 per kilometer;

• Pension accrual through Adecco from age 18;

• Access to the Adecco Academy for training and courses;

• A pleasant, safe work environment with dedicated colleagues.

Where will you work?
FedEx is one of the world's largest logistics service providers, shipping millions of packages daily from Duiven to over 200 countries. Working safely, collaborating, and continuously growing are our top priorities. Your efforts are recognized and appreciated.

What do we ask?
• You speak Dutch or English fluently;

• You can apply for a Certificate of Conduct (costs will be reimbursed);

• You have your own transportation;

• You can be deployed flexible.

Are you interested?
Ready to get started? Click the application button and take the next step in your career!

Questions? Send a message or call Sanne at 06 42506892. You can apply for this position until October 31st, 2026.

As a Production Employee at Bavaria in Lieshout, you will play an important role in brewing and packaging one of the Netherlands' most iconic beers. In our state-of-the-art bottling facility, you help fill approximately 100,000 cans and bottles every hour.

Working at Bavaria means being involved in the entire production process. Together with your colleagues, you ensure that production runs as smoothly and efficiently as possible. Your shift starts and ends with a handover, where you discuss production results, breakdowns, and other important details with operators from the other teams.

At Bavaria, you will enjoy a varied role with responsibilities including:

- Setting up and adjusting machines;
- Troubleshooting common technical issues;
- Performing maintenance on the production line;
- Sorting returnable bottles;
- Supplying packaging machines with caps and rolls;
- Monitoring and checking beer quality.

Working Hours & Availability

Until January, you will work in a fixed 3-shift rotation with a repeating three-week cycle:

- Week 1: 4 to 5 night shifts from 10:00 PM to 06:00 AM
- Week 2: 3 afternoon shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM and 2 morning shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM
- Week 3: 3 morning shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM and 2 afternoon shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM

From January onwards, you will transition to a fixed 5-shift rotation schedule:

- 2 early shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM
- 2 late shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM
- 2 night shifts from 10:00 PM to 06:00 AM
- 4 days off

Are you ready to become part of this dynamic family-owned company? Apply now and you could soon be working in the bottling facility of Royal Swinkels!

- You are available to work in a 5-shift rotation schedule and till januari in a 3-shift schedule; 
- You have a good command of either the Dutch or English language;
- You are eager to learn and develop new skills.
